{"records":[{"id":"ymn3ykkmyx","title":"A systematic CRISPR screen defines mutational mechanisms underpinning signatures caused by replication errors and endogenous DNA damage","description":"Mutational signatures are imprints of pathophysiological processes arising through tumorigenesis. We generated isogenic CRISPR–Cas9 knockouts (∆) of 43 genes in human induced pluripotent stem cells, cultured them in the absence of added DNA damage and performed whole-genome sequencing of 173 subclones. ∆OGG1, ∆UNG, ∆EXO1, ∆RNF168, ∆MLH1, ∆MSH2, ∆MSH6, ∆PMS1 and ∆PMS2 produced marked mutational signatures indicative of them being critical mitigators of endogenous DNA modifications. Detailed analyses revealed mutational mechanistic insights, including how 8-oxo-2′-deoxyguanosine elimination is sequence context specific while uracil clearance is sequence context independent. Mismatch repair (MMR) deficiency signatures are engendered by oxidative damage (C > A transversions) and differential misincorporation by replicative polymerases (T > C and C > T transitions), and we propose a reverse template slippage model for T > A transversions. ∆MLH1, ∆MSH6 and ∆MSH2 signatures were similar to each other but distinct from ∆PMS2. Finally, we developed a classifier, MMRDetect, where application to 7,695 whole-genome-sequenced cancers showed enhanced detection of MMR-deficient tumors, with implications for responsiveness to immunotherapies.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-04-19T14:39:59.262Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/ymn3ykkmyx","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/ymn3ykkmyx"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Serena","last_name":"Nik-Zainal","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Genomics","Cancer Genetics","CRISPR/Cas9"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"y8dndzn3mg","title":"Genome-scale CRISPR screen identifies TMEM41B as a critical host factor required for coronavirus replication","description":"These data are part of the Supplemental Items associated with the manuscript entitled \"Genome-scale CRISPR screen identifies TMEM41B as a critical host factor required for coronavirus replication\". These files include Supplementary Data file 1-4.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-03-16T10:34:13.579Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/y8dndzn3mg","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/y8dndzn3mg"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Limeng","last_name":"Sun","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Virus","Screening","CRISPR/Cas9"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"2v5jg2zksj","title":"TMEM79/MATTRIN defines a pathway for Frizzled regulation and is required for Xenopus embryogenesis","description":"Absctract\nWnt signaling through the Frizzled (FZD) family of serpentine receptors is essential for embryogenesis and homeostasis, and stringent control of the FZD protein level is critical for stem cell regulation. Through CRISPR/Cas9 genome-wide screening in human cells, we identified TMEM79/MATTRIN, an orphan multi-span transmembrane protein, as a specific inhibitor of Wnt/FZD signaling. TMEM79 interacts with FZD during biogenesis and promotes FZD degradation independent of ZNRF3/RNF43 ubiquitin ligases (R-spondin receptors). TMEM79 interacts with ubiquitin-specific protease 8 (USP8), whose activating mutations underlie human tumorigenesis. TMEM79 specifically inhibits USP8 deubiquitination of FZD, thereby governing USP8 substrate specificity and promoting FZD degradation. Tmem79 and Usp8 genes have a pre-bilaterian origin, and Tmem79 inhibition of Usp8 and Wnt signaling is required for anterior neural development and gastrulation in Xenopus embryos. TMEM79 is a predisposition gene for Atopic dermatitis, suggesting deregulation of Wnt/FZD signaling a possible cause for this most common yet enigmatic inflammatory skin disease.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-09-26T05:47:58.606Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/2v5jg2zksj","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/2v5jg2zksj"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Maorong","last_name":"Chen","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Nathalia","last_name":"Amado","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Jieqiong","last_name":"Tan","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Alice ","last_name":"Reis","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Mengxu","last_name":"Ge","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Jose","last_name":"Abreu","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Xi","last_name":"He","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Biochemistry","Molecular Biology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"ztg7pxr6ch","title":"STT3A is essential for Wnt signaling and represents a target for cancers driven by RNF43 deficiency","description":"This dataset contains the original raw and analyzed data supporting the manuscript “STT3A is essential for Wnt signaling and represents a target for cancers driven by RNF43 deficiency”. The study identifies STT3A as an essential regulator of the Wnt signaling pathway and a potential therapeutic target for RNF43-deficient cancers. Included data were generated from key experiments, including Wnt reporter assays (DDT), Western blotting (WB), and CRISPR screen, and other experiments central to the study","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-10-13T11:26:58.874Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/ztg7pxr6ch","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/ztg7pxr6ch"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Zhengjin","last_name":"He","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Cell Biology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"d5vw9sjcrv","title":"A target expression threshold dictates invader defense  and autoimmunity by CRISPR-Cas13","description":"Immune systems must recognize and clear foreign invaders without eliciting autoimmunity. CRISPR-Cas immune systems in prokaryotes manage this task by following two criteria: extensive guide:target complementarity and a defined target-flanking motif. Here we report an additional requirement for RNA-targeting CRISPR-Cas13 systems: expression of the target transcript exceeding a threshold. This finding is based on targeting endogenous non-essential transcripts, which rarely elicited dormancy through collateral RNA degradation. Instead, eliciting dormancy required over-expressing targeted transcripts above a threshold. A genome-wide screen confirmed target expression levels as the principal determinant of cytotoxic autoimmunity and revealed that the threshold shifts with the guide:target pair. This expression threshold ensured defense against a lytic bacteriophage yet allowed tolerance of a targeted beneficial gene expressed from an invading plasmid. These findings establish target expression levels as a third criterion for immune defense by RNA-targeting CRISPR-Cas systems, buffering against autoimmunity and distinguishing pathogenic and benign invaders.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-06-08T11:55:48.983Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/d5vw9sjcrv","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/d5vw9sjcrv"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Elena","last_name":"Vialetto","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Yanying","last_name":"Yu","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Scott","last_name":"Collins","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Katharina","last_name":"Wandera","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Lars","last_name":"Barquist","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Chase","last_name":"Beisel","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Data Analysis","Data Access"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"4mb5kjywkj","title":"Western Blot raw data of the manuscript titled \"In vivo CRISPR knockout screen identifies p47 as a suppressor for HER2+ breast cancer metastasis by regulating NEMO trafficking and autophagy flux\"","description":"The raw images of WB is for the reviewers' request when reviewing the manuscript titled \"In vivo CRISPR knockout screen identifies p47 as a suppressor for HER2+ breast cancer metastasis by regulating NEMO trafficking and autophagy flux\".","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-12-04T00:26:32.621Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/4mb5kjywkj","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/4mb5kjywkj"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Mingang","last_name":"Hao","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Western Blot"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"f7btcr6x6d","title":"A non-canonical function of glutathione to suppress ferroptosis via FSP1","description":"Whole genome-wide CRISPR KO screen","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-10-02T11:41:52.925Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/f7btcr6x6d","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/f7btcr6x6d"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"BO","last_name":"CHU","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Cell Biology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"zkjm36wp8s","title":"An Inter-Organ Neural Circuit for Appetite Suppression","description":"Glucagon-like peptide-1 (GLP-1) is a signal peptide released from enteroendocrine cells of the lower intestine. GLP-1 exerts anorectic and antimotility actions that protect the body against nutrient malabsorption. However, little is known about how intestinal GLP-1 affects distant organs despite rapid enzymatic inactivation. We show that intestinal GLP-1 inhibits gastric emptying and eating via intestinofugal neurons, a subclass of myenteric neurons that project to abdominal sympathetic ganglia. Remarkably, cell-specific ablation of intestinofugal neurons eliminated intestinal GLP-1 effects, and their chemical activation functioned as a GLP-1 mimetic. GLP-1 sensing by intestinofugal neurons then engaged a sympatho-gastro-spinal-reticular-hypothalamic pathway that links abnormal stomach distension to craniofacial programs for food rejection. Within this pathway, cell-specific activation of sparse neuronal populations caused systemic GLP-1-like effects. These molecularly identified, delimited enteric circuits may be targeted to ameliorate the abdominal bloating and loss of appetite typical of gastric motility disorders.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-06-06T17:19:00.612Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/zkjm36wp8s","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/zkjm36wp8s"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Wenfei","last_name":"Han","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Neuroscience","Gut Endocrinology","Resource"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"66ms37y66x","title":"Data for: A genome-wide CRISPR/Cas9 screen reveals that riboflavin regulates hydrogen peroxide entry into HAP1 cells  ","description":"CRISPR screen data for hydrogen peroxide mediated cell death","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-02-13T14:30:16.414Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/66ms37y66x","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/66ms37y66x"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"surachai","last_name":"supattapone","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Kenneth","last_name":"Mark","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Tamutenda","last_name":"Chidawanyika","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Oxidative Stress"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"65pfcj4j4m","title":"Protocol of CRISPR-Cas9 knockout screens for identifying ferroptosis regulators","description":"Ferroptosis, an iron-dependent programmed cell death triggered by excessive lipid peroxidation, has shown promising therapeutic potentials in human diseases. Here, we describe a protocol of a CRISPR-Cas9 loss-of-function screen to identify regulators in response to different inducers of ferroptosis. We emphasize the steps of library amplification, drug treatment, high-throughput sequencing preparation, and bioinformatics analysis using Model-based Analysis of Genome-wide CRISPR-Cas9 Knockout (MAGeCK). We also present a method to discover the regulators of ferroptosis and verify the potential targets efficiently.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-10-24T01:46:48.793Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/65pfcj4j4m","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/65pfcj4j4m"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Xin","last_name":"Yang","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Wei","last_name":"Gu","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["CRISPR/Cas9","Ferroptosis"],"journal_issn":[]}],"total_records":92675,"page":1,"page_size":10,"execution_time":85,"aggregations":{"data_type_stats":{"dataset":92675,"collection":0},"access_type_stats":{"open":92406,"restricted":51,"embargoed":218},"top_funders_stats":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01h0zpd94","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","count":1564},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","count":512},{"id":"https://ror.org/03ha2q922","name":"National Science Centre","count":373},{"id":"https://ror.org/02ddkpn78","name":"Fundação de Amparo à Pesquisa do Estado de São Paulo","count":323},{"id":"https://ror.org/03swz6y49","name":"National Council for Scientific and Technological Development","count":311},{"id":"https://ror.org/00x0ma614","name":"Coordenação de Aperfeicoamento de Pessoal de Nível Superior","count":308},{"id":"https://ror.org/021nxhr62","name":"U.S. National Science Foundation","count":285},{"id":"https://ror.org/018mejw64","name":"Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft","count":265},{"id":"https://ror.org/00hhkn466","name":"Japan Society for the Promotion of Science","count":193},{"id":"https://ror.org/00k4n6c32","name":"European Commission","count":178}],"source_stats":[{"id":"MENDELEY_DATA","name":"Mendeley Data","count":90362},{"id":"f881433a-b1cd-40d2-ab9f-4fd501f2d14b","name":"Elsevier Data Repository","count":1747},{"id":"a191461c-0227-403f-a1e9-621e0e0429cc","name":"San Raffaele Open Research Data Repository","count":159},{"id":"b07018a5-fee6-4df1-9d43-ff0d81ad75ed","name":"Bicocca Open Archive Research Data","count":89},{"id":"2a9d1b7d-e447-466f-888f-aa6f84e575e4","name":"Digital Commons Data@Becker","count":59},{"id":"df228bbb-ac66-410f-8c66-f61608d63d95","name":"University of South Florida","count":54},{"id":"72c28c45-627f-446b-8a48-af7c0a51a357","name":"Università Cattolica del Sacro Cuore","count":47},{"id":"b121dfec-bb51-4f19-a2f6-bc9ce0197286","name":"Babeș-Bolyai University","count":31},{"id":"7e51a2dd-133e-43c6-a220-12c1958e202a","name":"University of Canberra","count":26},{"id":"5f1edf21-7948-4d82-894f-c0ed4b1e8f52","name":"Teesside University","count":25}],"top_institutions_stats":[{"id":"3bfef41a-d03e-5722-bd55-dd245235fa78","name":"Bina Nusantara University","count":408},{"id":"0ad97c43-5173-56e6-bbe6-46dad5323862","name":"Daffodil International University","count":369},{"id":"f58d7a83-6efa-5d8a-a6c2-b9e78ee14783","name":"Maharishi Markandeshwar Institute of Physiotherapy and Rehabilitation","count":319},{"id":"55ba66b2-f276-5204-a3d8-acfa499794e0","name":"The University of Manchester","count":242},{"id":"48c8fa0f-965c-5cbf-a859-a5363432478b","name":"Universidade de Sao Paulo","count":236}]}}